@startuml
!theme plain
title D04 optimisation job status

[*] --> PENDING : POST /jobs/plan\nrow committed, engine not yet called

PENDING --> PROCESSING : dispatch answered 202
PENDING --> FAILED : engine unreachable,\nnon-202 answer, or any dispatch exception

PROCESSING --> COMPLETED : POST /callbacks/complete\nsolution persisted, orders updated
PROCESSING --> FAILED : POST /callbacks/failed
PROCESSING --> CANCELLED : PUT /jobs\n(Entry writes CANCELLED, then asks the engine)
PROCESSING --> CANCELLED : POST /callbacks/cancelled

FAILED --> COMPLETED : POST /callbacks/complete\n(accepted on purpose: a job marked FAILED by a\nprocessing error must still accept the replay)

COMPLETED --> COMPLETED : duplicate completion\n(idempotent no-op)
CANCELLED --> CANCELLED : late completion or failure\n(ignored)
FAILED --> FAILED : duplicate failure\n(no-op)

note right of PENDING
  A completion callback that arrives while the row is
  still PENDING is answered 503, not 200: the engine
  keeps the payload and retries after about 60 s, by
  which time the dispatch has set PROCESSING.
end note

note bottom
  There is no transition out of FAILED other than a
  completion callback, and no automatic retry of
  dispatch. A cancelled job never returns to the queue.
  canBeCancelled() == (status == PROCESSING) is the only
  guard the cancel endpoint uses.
end note
@enduml
